---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const ctaMailto = 'mailto:eric@ericangella.com?subject=Claim%20My%20Free%20LinkedIn%20Workover';

// Update this each time capacity resets.
const availableSlots = 1;
const openDate = 'TBD'; // e.g. "September 2026"
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Free LinkedIn Workover — Eric Angella"
  description="A free, hands-on rework of your LinkedIn profile — limited to a small number of people."
>
  <a href="/work" class="back">← Work</a>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="lp-hero">
    <h1>Your knowledge is valuable.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      But the people who could use it can't find it on your LinkedIn profile.
      Or know what to do next after they land on it.
    </p>
    <p class="lp-body">
      I built a tool that closes that gap. For a limited number of people,
      I'll run it on your profile for free.
    </p>
    <p class="lp-availability">{availableSlots} available as of {openDate}</p>
    <a href={ctaMailto} class="btn-primary">Claim Your Free Workover →</a>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- THE PROBLEM -->
  <p class="section-label">The Problem</p>
  <h2 class="lp-h2">You Know Things Most People Don't.</h2>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">
    You've solved problems, made calls under pressure, built things that
    worked. None of that is on your profile.
  </p>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">
    What's there instead is a job title, a list of duties, and a summary
    that could belong to a thousand other people. Anyone who lands on that
    profile scrolls past it, confused about what you actually do.
  </p>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">
    There's a newer wrinkle too: LinkedIn uses your profile to decide who
    sees your posts. A vague profile sends a vague signal, and the
    algorithm has nothing clear to route your content toward. So a generic
    profile costs you twice — once with anyone who lands on it, and again
    every time you post.
  </p>
  <blockquote class="lp-quote">I call it your Authority Gap.</blockquote>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">
    It's the distance between what you know and what you've actually said
    publicly. It's costing you the recognition, the inbound conversations,
    and the opportunities that go to people who are simply louder about
    less.
  </p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- THE OFFER -->
  <p class="section-label">The Offer</p>
  <h2 class="lp-h2">A Free, Hands-On Rework</h2>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">
    I'm finishing a LinkedIn Workover tool and opening it to a small number
    of people before it's public. You get a free, hands-on rework of your
    profile. I get to watch it work on a real profile and hear what you
    think.
  </p>

  <div class="lp-fit-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="lp-fit-label">What you get</p>
      <ul class="lp-plain-list">
        <li>A full pass on your headline, About section, and experience narrative</li>
        <li>A clear pathway for others to work with you ("call to action")</li>
        <li>A clear read on what's currently hiding your expertise instead of showing it</li>
        <li>Specific, usable rewrites, not generic advice</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="lp-fit-label">What it costs you</p>
      <ul class="lp-plain-list">
        <li>About the time it takes to answer a short set of questions and give me honest feedback afterward</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max lp-italic">That's it. No pitch at the end, no obligation.</p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- WHY FREE -->
  <p class="section-label">Why Free</p>
  <h2 class="lp-h2">Because It Isn't Finished Yet.</h2>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">
    The only way to finish it right is to run it on real people with real
    profiles. I'd rather trade the work for your honest reaction than guess
    what's missing.
  </p>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">If it's not useful to you, I want to know that too.</p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- WHO THIS IS FOR -->
  <p class="section-label">Who This Is For</p>
  <h2 class="lp-h2">Depth Without a Profile That Shows It.</h2>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">
    This works best for technical founders, CTOs, VPs of Engineering, and
    product leaders — people with real depth who've never had the time, or
    the interest, in translating it into a profile that shows it.
  </p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- CAPACITY -->
  <p class="section-label">Capacity</p>
  <h2 class="lp-h2">Five, Rolling.</h2>
  <p class="lp-body lp-max">
    I'm only taking 5 of these on a rolling basis, run personally, one at a
    time. Once they're booked, the next round opens later.
  </p>
  <a href={ctaMailto} class="btn-primary">Claim Your Free Workover →</a>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <p class="section-label">FAQ</p>
  <h2 class="lp-h2">A Few Questions</h2>

  <div class="lp-faq-list">
    <div class="lp-faq-item">
      <p class="lp-faq-q">Is this really free?</p>
      <p class="lp-faq-a">Yes. In exchange, I ask for honest feedback after — what worked, what didn't, what you'd pay for.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lp-faq-item">
      <p class="lp-faq-q">What if I'm not ready to publish anything yet?</p>
      <p class="lp-faq-a">Fine. This is about seeing what's possible, not committing to anything.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lp-faq-item">
      <p class="lp-faq-q">Do you keep doing this after the tool launches?</p>
      <p class="lp-faq-a">No. This free round is limited to the current group. After that, it becomes part of the paid offering.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .back {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 60px;
  }
  .back:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .lp-max {
    max-width: 560px;
  }

  .lp-hero {
    padding: 20px 0 0;
  }
  .lp-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(38px, 7vw, 56px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    max-width: 600px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    max-width: 520px;
  }
  .lp-body {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .lp-italic {
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .lp-availability {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }

  .lp-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 4.5vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 4px 0 22px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--text);
    color: var(--bg);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 14px 26px;
    margin: 8px 0 44px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    opacity: 0.85;
    color: var(--bg);
  }

  .lp-quote {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--line);
    padding-left: 22px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 30px 0;
  }

  .lp-fit-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 50px;
    margin: 26px 0;
  }
  .lp-fit-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .lp-plain-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .lp-plain-list li {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding: 8px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .lp-plain-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .lp-faq-list {
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  .lp-faq-item {
    padding: 26px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .lp-faq-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .lp-faq-q {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 19px;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .lp-faq-a {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 540px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .lp-fit-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 30px;
    }
  }
</style>
